  data: {
    LLM: "Keep track of which numbers are 'open'. Avoid being the one who has to draw and pay chips into the pool.\n\nThe Auction Decision: Bid for the last two tiles if your hand is nearly complete and needs 'flexibility' (new numbers), or if you want to prevent an opponent from potentially winning.\n\nValue of Information: In the auction, if you hold most of the remaining 5s and 6s, and the board has open 5s and 6s, the auction tiles are less valuable to you because you already control those paths.",
    Player: "Keep track of which numbers are 'open'. Avoid being the one who has to draw and pay chips into the pool.\n\nThe Auction Decision: Bid for the last two tiles if your hand is nearly complete and needs 'flexibility' (new numbers), or if you want to prevent an opponent from potentially winning.\n\nValue of Information: In the auction, if you hold most of the remaining 5s and 6s, and the board has open 5s and 6s, the auction tiles are less valuable to you because you already control those paths.",
